//? Title: FactorVAE and betaTCVAE: Two Ways to Penalize Latent Dependence
//? Subtitle: Alternating density-ratio fitting versus a complete empirical Gaussian mixture
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Total correlation measures dependence among latent coordinates. This report compares a learned
joint-versus-product discriminator with an exact finite-mixture calculation, keeping the same
compact Gaussian VAE, initial arrays, minibatch order and explicit noise banks. On294 unique
binary circle/square images, each VAE receives21 Adam updates; FactorVAE also receives21
separate discriminator updates. Common four-draw validation NLL+analytic KL selects each
checkpoint. Both select epoch3, but decode(mu) test MSE0.08413/0.07537 is worse than the
fitting-only mean0.04855. Unfiltered predictions, prior codes, traversals and heldout probes
retain that limitation. This small run is a mechanism demonstration, not evidence of
successful disentanglement or a reproduction of either paper's benchmark.
)
\toc

> From the aggregated posterior to two TC surrogates

The encoder gives q(z|x)=N(mu(x),diag(exp(l(x)))); supplied independent standard-normal
noise makes z=mu+exp(l/2)⊙epsilon differentiable. A784→32ReLU encoder feeds two linear
four-coordinate heads;4→32ReLU→784 logits form a sample-only Bernoulli decoder. Pixels
are summed, latent coordinates are summed, and images are averaged. With logit a,
R(x,z)=sum_j[softplus(a_j)−x_j a_j] and K(x)=0.5 sum_d[mu_d²+exp(l_d)−1−l_d].
The unweighted VAE loss estimates the negative ELBO from
[Kingma and Welling](https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6114).

For aggregated q(z)=E_x q(z|x), total correlation is

$$
\mathrm{TC}(q)=D_{\rm KL}\!\left(q(z)\;\middle\|\;\prod_d q(z_d)\right)
=E_{q(z)}\!\left[\log q(z)-\sum_d\log q(z_d)\right].
$$
\alttext(Total correlation compares the joint aggregated posterior with the product of its one-coordinate marginals.)

A factorized conditional q(z|x) can still have a dependent aggregated posterior: different
images move several means together. Penalizing every conditional KL is therefore different
from explicitly penalizing TC. [Kim and Mnih's FactorVAE](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v80/kim18b.html)
learns the density ratio using joint samples versus independently shuffled latent columns.
[Chen et al.'s betaTCVAE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.04942) separates TC from the other
aggregated-posterior terms. This report's betaTC variant uses **all210 fitting posteriors as
an equally weighted finite mixture**, rather than the paper's minibatch estimator.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tc_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
