> Selected results, controls and unfiltered predictions

Both models select epoch3. FactorVAE test NLL250.710/KL30.746 gives common281.457nats/image;
betaTC NLL240.147/KL31.101 gives271.249. Weighted objectives280.714/271.890 are distinct
from their common selection scores. Decode(mu) MSE0.08413/0.07537 is worse than the
fitting-only pixel mean0.04855. Three short epochs do not give good reconstructions.
The following curve uses only completed-epoch validation, with no epoch-zero candidate.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tc_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (const std::string name : {"factor_vae", "beta_tcvae"}) {
    std::ifstream f("build/tc_vae/" + name + "/history.tsv");
    std::string   line;
    std::getline(f, line);
    std::vector<double> epochs, scores;
    while (std::getline(f, line)) {
      std::istringstream r(line);
      double             e, fit, nll, kl, common, weighted;
      r >> e >> fit >> nll >> kl >> common >> weighted;
      epochs.push_back(e);
      scores.push_back(common);
    }
    chart.lines(
        epochs,
        scores,
        name,
        name == "factor_vae" ? dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235} : dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38},
        2);
  }
  chart.title("Common four-draw validation NLL + KL")
      .x_label("completed epoch")
      .y_label("nats per image")
      .save_svg("build/tc_learning.svg");
}
