The20 prior codes are identical for both models. Traversals vary one coordinate by−2,−1.5,…,2
around that model's fitting posterior mean, holding the others fixed; each model contributes
four rows of nine. These are decoder probabilities, not sampled binary images. Traversing a
coordinate does not identify it with a true generative factor.

