> Fitting-only probes and reproducibility boundaries

LatentFactorDiagnostics fits population centering/scales on fitting mu, standardized ridge
penalty0.001, and one-axis probes chosen by maximum absolute **fitting** correlation (lowest
axis wins ties). Factor targets are numeric shape/size/x/y indices. The heldout mean enters
only the R² denominator. No heldout target chooses coefficients, scales or axes. Negative R²
remains visible. The13-array archive also retains fitting mean/std, variance, per-unit KL,
fit/test correlations, coefficients, selected axes and both heldout predictions.
These are descriptive probes, not MIG/DCI, paper benchmark scores or proof of disentanglement.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::print("| model | ridge R2 shape | size | x | y |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (const std::string model : {"factor_vae", "beta_tcvae"})
    for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz("build/tc_vae/" + model + "/factor_probes.npz"))
      if (key == "ridge_r2") {
        const auto v = value.to_vector<double>();
        std::print("| {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n", model, v[0], v[1], v[2], v[3]);
      }
}
```
